<section class="booksy-alt__section" aria-labelledby="booksy-alt-decision-title">
  <div class="booksy-alt__glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="booksy-alt__intro">
      <h2 id="booksy-alt-decision-title" class="booksy-alt__h2">
        So, which approach fits your barbershop?
      </h2>
    </header>

    <div class="booksy-alt-panels">
      <article class="booksy-alt-panel">
        <p class="booksy-alt-panel__label">BOOKSY MAY SUIT YOU IF…</p>
        <ul class="booksy-alt-panel__list">
          <li>Marketplace discovery is central to how you attract new clients.</li>
          <li>You specifically want the Booksy consumer app and marketplace ecosystem.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="booksy-alt-panel booksy-alt-panel--kersivo">
        <p class="booksy-alt-panel__label">KERSIVO MAY SUIT YOU IF…</p>
        <ul class="booksy-alt-panel__list">
          <li>You want your own branded website and standard domain included.</li>
          <li>You want bookings to stay centred on your business and brand.</li>
          <li>You want 0% KERSIVO commission on bookings and retail sales.</li>
          <li>You want your barber team managed within one location plan.</li>
          <li>
            You want deposits, automated reminders, client management and retail pickup in one
            platform.
          </li>
          <li>You want help moving from your current booking system.</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="booksy-alt-closing">
      Neither model is right for every barbershop. The real question is whether you want your booking
      journey built around a marketplace ecosystem or around your own barbershop.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
